<div class="card doc" id="live"><div class="card-h"><h3><?=icon('book')?>Go live – step by step (shared hosting / cPanel / Hostinger)</h3></div>
<h4>1. Requirements</h4><ul class="ul"><li>PHP 8.0+ with extensions: <code>pdo_mysql</code>, <code>curl</code>, <code>mbstring</code>, <code>dom</code>, <code>gd</code>, <code>zip</code>, <code>openssl</code> (all standard on cPanel/Hostinger). Your server: PHP <b><?=PHP_VERSION?></b><?php foreach(['pdo_mysql','curl','mbstring','dom','gd','zip','openssl'] as $x):?> · <?=$x?> <?=extension_loaded($x)?'✅':'❌'?><?php endforeach?></li><li>MySQL 5.7+ / MariaDB 10.3+ database.</li><li>SSL certificate (free Let's Encrypt in cPanel) – needed so WhatsApp can fetch the PDF link.</li></ul>
<h4>2. Upload the files</h4><ul class="ul"><li><b>Option A (easiest):</b> On GitHub open <code>github.com/narendersinghh/Setu-crm</code> → Releases → download the latest release ZIP (or Code → Download ZIP). In cPanel → File Manager, open <code>public_html</code> (or a sub-folder / sub-domain like <code>leads.yourdomain.com</code>), Upload the ZIP and Extract. Move the files out of the <code>Setu-crm-…</code> folder if needed.</li><li><b>Option B:</b> cPanel → Git™ Version Control → Create → Clone URL <code>https://github.com/narendersinghh/Setu-crm.git</code>, then deploy into your web folder.</li></ul>
<h4>3. Create the database</h4><ul class="ul"><li>cPanel → MySQL® Database Wizard: create a database, a user with a strong password, and grant <b>ALL PRIVILEGES</b>.</li></ul>
<h4>4. Run the installer</h4><ul class="ul"><li>Visit <code><?=e(base_url('install.php'))?></code>, enter the database details and create your admin login. It creates <code>config.php</code> and all tables.</li><li>Make sure the <code>storage/</code> and <code>assets/uploads/</code> folders are writable (permission 755 – or 775 if needed).</li></ul>
<?php $cm=Cron::mode();?><h4 id="cron">5. Background scheduler – automatic</h4><p>No setup needed. Setu runs its background work (searching, audits, AI reports, sending, reply detection) by itself: it adds a server cron job automatically when your host allows it, otherwise its built-in scheduler keeps running and restarts itself whenever someone opens the app, a report link or a webhook arrives.</p><p>Status: <?=$cm==='server'?'<span class="bdg bdg-green">Running – server cron</span>':($cm==='web'?'<span class="bdg bdg-green">Running – built-in scheduler</span>':'<span class="bdg bdg-red">Not running</span>')?> <span class="muted">last run <?=$cron?ago(date('Y-m-d H:i:s',$cron)):'never'?></span></p><div class="row"><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="a" value="cron_kick"><button class="btn btn-sm"><?=icon('play')?>Start / restart scheduler</button></form><?php if($cm!=='server'):?><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="a" value="cron_install"><button class="btn btn-sm"><?=icon('clock')?>Try adding server cron automatically</button></form><?php endif?></div><p class="hint">Optional, for maximum reliability: hPanel → Advanced → Cron Jobs → every minute → <code><?=e(Cron::cmd())?></code></p><h4>6. Connect services</h4><ul class="ul"><li><b>AI Connection</b> tab → add your Claude / ChatGPT / OpenRouter / Gemini key and click Test.</li><li><b>Settings → Map scraper &amp; audits</b> → Google Places API key (or SerpAPI key).</li><li><b>Settings → Email</b> → SMTP of your domain mailbox (e.g. from cPanel → Email Accounts → Connect Devices) + IMAP for reply tracking.</li><li><b>Settings → WhatsApp</b> → Manual mode works instantly; for automatic sending connect WhatsApp Cloud API and set webhook <code><?=e(base_url('webhook.php'))?></code>.</li><li><b>Settings → Company / Report branding / Pricing</b> → your logo, colours, fonts, fees and website proposal PDF.</li><li><b>Settings → Lead capture</b> → connect website forms, Meta lead ads, Google Ads lead forms and webhooks.</li><li><b>Settings → AI voice calls</b> → Sarvam AI, Bland, Vapi or Retell for automatic calls.</li></ul>
<h4>7. Updating later</h4><ul class="ul"><li>This tab checks GitHub automatically (every 6 hours) and shows a <b>New</b> badge in the sidebar. Click <b>Update now</b> – new files are installed and the database is migrated. <code>config.php</code>, <code>storage/</code> (reports, uploads, logs, backups) and your database data are never overwritten.</li><li>To publish an update: bump <code>VERSION</code> and <code>version.json</code>, push, then create a GitHub release with the same tag (e.g. <code>v1.1.0</code>). Sites on <b>Releases only</b> get it then; sites on <b>Latest commit</b> get every push.</li></ul>
<h4>Security tips</h4><ul class="ul"><li>Use HTTPS, a strong admin password, and keep <code>config.php</code> private (it is protected by <code>.htaccess</code>).</li><li>On Nginx hosts (no .htaccess), block access to <code>/app</code>, <code>/storage</code> and <code>config.php</code> in the server config.</li><li>Respect anti-spam rules: keep the daily limit and gap between sends reasonable, and stop contacting anyone who asks you to.</li></ul></div>
